/AC4; test file tests/unit/test_mcp_startup_sweep_background.py","norm_id":"n3fea67e9cc304de9","priority":0.875,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["run_ensures patched to raise: the server must remain serving and the gauge must return to 0 (finally release), else shutdown drain blocks indefinitely."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Extend the regression test with a case where run_ensures raises, asserting the process does not abort, the gauge returns to 0, and wait_for_idle returns.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.875,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"uncertifiable_outcome","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"Justify (or preserve) the fail-closed behaviour for a RemovedInputError raised INSIDE run_ensures on the background thread — either establish that no ensure unit can raise it (only tracker resolution can, which stays synchronous) or have the thread signal a fatal abort (e.g. set server.should_exit / os._exit) rather than demoting it to an error-log.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.0044,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_deprecations.py:77 `class RemovedInputError(BaseException)` — chosen as BaseException so it bypasses broad `except Exception` handlers and aborts; current synchronous run_startup_store_sweep re-raises it to fail MCP boot hard","Plan: 'The existing exception handling moves into the thread unchanged: debug-log anything else, error-log a RemovedInputError that reaches the thread, since a thread cannot abort the process.'","AC4 only asserts the SYNCHRONOUS (tracker-resolution) RemovedInputError still propagates; it is silent on a RemovedInputError raised from inside run_ensures, which previously aborted boot"],"finding":"Backgrounding the sweep body downgrades a RemovedInputError raised INSIDE run_ensures from a hard boot-abort (its current behaviour, since RemovedInputError is a BaseException that survives the broad handler and propagates out of main()) to a mere error-log, because a daemon thread cannot abort the process. The plan resolves the tracker path synchronously to preserve the config-origin abort, but does not justify why a RemovedInputError originating in an ensure unit may safely be demoted to a log line and the server allowed to keep serving.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0d3f6f9036058dfd","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 ('error-log a RemovedInputError that reaches the thread, since a thread cannot abort the process') and AC4","norm_id":"ncf7457d467a1f272","priority":0.5956,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A load-bearing input is removed but still set, and the removal is surfaced by an ensure unit (not by tracker_dir() resolution): pre-fix the MCP container fails to boot (fail-closed); post-fix it logs an error and serves"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"medium","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["2 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Specify operator-visible signaling for background sweep failure (e.g. warn/error-log or a metric when the background ensure sweep does not complete cleanly), not only debug-log.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5a","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The existing exception handling moves into the thread unchanged: debug-log anything else, error-log a RemovedInputError that reaches the thread'","Previously the sweep ran synchronously BEFORE serving, so a failure (or non-convergence) was observable before uvicorn started"],"finding":"Moving the sweep to a background daemon thread converts a previously-synchronous boot-blocking failure into a debug-logged, invisible one: a non-RemovedInputError ensure failure is only debug-logged, so a persistently non-converging store sweep becomes undetectable at normal log levels after the server is already serving.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f4608d5c80786b5f1","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1 (sweep body / exception handling)","norm_id":"n8aaaa8be0a82bdb5","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After restart the background sweep repeatedly fails or times out (timeout=5, attempts=1); the server serves fine but the store stays un-swept and operators see only a debug-level line"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Keep RemovedInputError at error level, but raise non-RemovedInputError sweep failures/timeouts to warning (or record them on the gauge/a counter) so a persistently failing background sweep is observable.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State the failure-disposition when the background sweep fails: is serving an un-ensured store an accepted degraded (non-fatal) disposition, and how is that surfaced beyond a debug/error log?","cohort":["E3","E5","G5","T12","T6","T9","necessity","project.engine-layer-enforcement","project.failure-disposition-contract","project.portability"],"criteria":["project.failure-disposition-contract"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.801,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["'The existing exception handling moves into the thread unchanged: debug-log anything else, error-log a RemovedInputError that reaches the thread, since a thread cannot abort the process.'","Pre-fix, a RemovedInputError in the synchronous sweep aborted process startup; post-fix the thread cannot abort, so the server keeps serving."],"finding":"The plan moves the sweep's exception handling into the background thread ('debug-log anything else, error-log a RemovedInputError that reaches the thread, since a thread cannot abort the process') but never states the disposition of the SERVICE when the background sweep fails entirely: the server now serves an un-swept/un-ensured store instead of aborting startup as it did before. Whether serving-with-a-failed-sweep is an accepted degraded disposition is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"ff8f5901e961ca5ca","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan step 1, sweep body exception handling","norm_id":"n5d31eb157426c471","priority":0.099,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["run_ensures raises inside the thread: the server answers MCP requests against a store whose ensure sweep never completed, with only a log line marking the degradation."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to step 1 stating that an in-thread sweep failure is a non-